- How to reconstruct the actual palindrome after deletions?
- How to optimize to O(n) space while keeping reconstruction capability?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests 1D partition DP, median-based block costs, and reconstruction; mirrors realistic facility placement.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions
- Median-based block cost
- Prefix sums for O(1) block cost
- Backpointer reconstruction
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function minPostOffice(X, k) {
  const n = X.length;
  const cost = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));

  // Precompute prefix sums for O(1) range sum queries
  const prefix = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] + X[i];
  }

  // Precompute block costs using median property
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      const m = Math.floor((l + r) / 2);
      cost[l][r] = (X[m] * (m - l) - (prefix[m] - prefix[l])) +
                   ((prefix[r + 1] - prefix[m + 1]) - X[m] * (r - m));
    }
  }

  // DP table and backpointers
  const dp = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n + 1}, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let p = 1; p <= k; p++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = p - 1; j < i; j++) {
        const candidate = dp[j][p - 1] + cost[j][i - 1];
        if (candidate < dp[i][p]) {
          dp[i][p] = candidate;
          parent[i][p] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct solution
  const blocks = [];
  let curr = n;
  for (let p = k; p >= 1; p--) {
    const start = parent[curr][p];
    blocks.unshift([start, curr - 1]);
    curr = start;
  }

  return { cost: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Complexity Analysis
- Time: O(kn²) for DP transitions plus O(n²) for cost preprocessing
- Space: O(nk) for DP table, reducible to O(n) with layer optimization

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP design for selecting multiple disjoint subarrays with reconstruction. Requires prefix sums, state definition, and backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- DP over positions and count of subarrays
- Prefix sums for subarray sums
- Reconstructing intervals with predecessor pointers
- Time/space trade-offs (O(nk) vs optimizations)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length; const P = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=1;i<=n;i++) P[i] = P[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const from = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>new Array(k+1).fill(null));
  for (let i=0;i<=n;i++) dp[i][0] = 0;
  for (let t=1;t<=k;t++){
    let best = -Infinity;
    let bestIdx = -1;
    for (let i=1;i<=n;i++){
      if (dp[i-1][t-1] - P[i-1] > best){ best = dp[i-1][t-1] - P[i-1]; bestIdx = i-1; }
      const take = P[i] + best;
      if (take > dp[i-1][t]){ dp[i][t] = take; from[i][t] = [bestIdx+1, i]; }
      else { dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t]; }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction (omitted for brevity in this snippet)
  return {maxSum: dp[n][k], intervals: []};
}
